WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:06.361
"Your Majesty, I'm impressed that you saved those people."

2
00:00:06.362 --> 00:00:11.042
Lord Hertford gathered up his papers from the advisers' meeting.

3
00:00:11.043 --> 00:00:15.298
"You showed real persistence in dealing with that sheriff.

4
00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:21.396
I heard many comments about how dignified and royal you appeared."

5
00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:29.837
"After questioning the sheriff and freeing those people, I feel more like a king," Tom said.

6
00:00:29.838 --> 00:00:35.659
"But I'm still a little nervous about dining in public today."

7
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:43.798
"Oh, I'm confident you'll do well at that—and at your coronation next month."

8
00:00:43.799 --> 00:00:46.704
"My coronation?"

9
00:00:46.705 --> 00:00:51.279
Tom hadn't thought about a coronation, but of course there would be one.

10
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:57.465
A king wasn't really a king until he received his crown in a long, boring ceremony.

11
00:00:57.466 --> 00:01:02.189
Father Andrew's books were full of coronations.

12
00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:05.289
Tom's stomach rumbled.

13
00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:09.521
Was that panic or was he just hungry?

14
00:01:09.522 --> 00:01:13.125
Tom gave Lord Hertford a weak smile.

15
00:01:13.126 --> 00:01:20.240
"Is it all right to postpone thinking about my coronation until after lunch?"

16
00:01:20.241 --> 00:01:25.535
Lord Hertford nodded. "Perfectly fine, Your Majesty."

17
00:01:25.536 --> 00:01:34.007
Tom straightened up so that he stood as tall as possible. "Then let's go!"

18
00:01:34.008 --> 00:01:41.609
That afternoon Tom felt remarkably calm in the palace's magnificent banquet hall.

19
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:46.760
A trumpeter sounded a horn as Tom took his seat.

20
00:01:46.761 --> 00:01:51.916
His table was on a raised platform so that everyone could watch him eat.

21
00:01:51.917 --> 00:01:56.573
Tom looked down at the people eager for him to begin eating.

22
00:01:56.574 --> 00:02:01.887
The whole purpose of this meal was to reassure everyone that he was in good health.

23
00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:06.217
"Now what am I supposed to do?" Tom thought.

24
00:02:06.218 --> 00:02:11.145
He closed his eyes, trying to recall his instructions from Lord Hertford.

25
00:02:11.146 --> 00:02:14.483
"Oh yes, now I remember."

26
00:02:14.484 --> 00:02:19.954
He nodded to his advisers and other people that he recognized.

27
00:02:19.955 --> 00:02:25.502
He allowed the royal napkin holder to tie a napkin around his neck.

28
00:02:25.503 --> 00:02:31.883
He waited patiently while the royal cupbearer filled his cup with water.

29
00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:39.331
Tom studied the forks, knives, and spoons while the royal taster performed his job.

30
00:02:39.332 --> 00:02:44.406
"There's a lot of silverware on this table," Tom thought.

31
00:02:44.407 --> 00:02:49.376
"I hope I remember which piece to use when."

32
00:02:49.377 --> 00:02:54.622
But then he thought of the rule he'd read in the royal etiquette book.

33
00:02:54.623 --> 00:03:00.531
"Always begin with the utensil farthest away from the plate."

34
00:03:00.532 --> 00:03:05.504
Tom smiled to himself and picked up the salad fork.

35
00:03:05.505 --> 00:03:09.869
Throughout the meal Tom was careful not to hurry.

36
00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:14.783
He didn't do anything for himself that a servant could do for him.

37
00:03:14.784 --> 00:03:19.691
As he started to reach for the butter, he stopped and looked at a servant.

38
00:03:19.692 --> 00:03:25.999
The man scurried to Tom's side and placed some butter on Tom's baked potato.

39
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.504
"Is that enough butter, Your Majesty?" the servant asked.

40
00:03:30.505 --> 00:03:33.392
Tom nodded.

41
00:03:33.393 --> 00:03:35.580
"Would you like some pepper?"

42
00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:40.892
The servant held a huge pepper mill over Tom's plate.

43
00:03:40.893 --> 00:03:47.669
Tom nodded again and thought about the days when he used to play at being a prince.

44
00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:53.285
"We never used to pretend we were having banquets," he thought.

45
00:03:53.286 --> 00:03:58.172
"It's hard to think about food when you're hungry."

46
00:03:58.173 --> 00:04:05.462
Tom's mouth watered while the servant cut up his meat and poured gravy over it.

47
00:04:05.463 --> 00:04:08.027
"I could have done that faster myself!"

48
00:04:08.028 --> 00:04:12.998
Tom thought as he quickly reached for a piece with the correct fork.

49
00:04:12.999 --> 00:04:20.308
Suddenly the meat slipped from the fork, hit Tom's lap, and bounced onto the floor.

50
00:04:20.309 --> 00:04:26.555
"Ohh!" Everyone in the room groaned and exchanged looks of dismay.

51
00:04:26.556 --> 00:04:31.976
Lord Hertford silently hoped that Tom would leave the meat alone.

52
00:04:31.977 --> 00:04:34.642
"Don't worry, I've got it!"

53
00:04:34.643 --> 00:04:39.907
Tom started to reach under the table before he remembered that kings shouldn't do that.

54
00:04:39.908 --> 00:04:43.636
"Just joking!"

55
00:04:43.637 --> 00:04:53.753
Everyone laughed, and Lord Hertford sighed with relief.

56
00:04:53.754 --> 00:05:00.004
The servant crawled under the table to remove the piece of meat.

57
00:05:00.005 --> 00:05:06.024
The royal napkin holder brought Tom a fresh napkin.

58
00:05:06.025 --> 00:05:12.546
"Nancy and I were so hungry, we would have fought over that meat," Tom thought.

59
00:05:12.547 --> 00:05:18.923
"I hope someone gets to eat it."

60
00:05:18.924 --> 00:05:21.913
The rest of the meal went perfectly.

61
00:05:21.914 --> 00:05:27.174
Tom even dared to ask for a third piece of chocolate cake.

62
00:05:27.175 --> 00:05:33.442
He washed his hands in rose water and wasn't even tempted to drink from the gold bowl.

63
00:05:33.443 --> 00:05:37.549
"That wasn't so hard," Tom thought as he stood up.

64
00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.910
And then he realized he had to burp.

65
00:05:40.911 --> 00:05:47.118
"Oh no!" he thought. "Is it rude for a king to burp in public?

66
00:05:47.119 --> 00:05:51.857
If only I had someone to do that for me!"

67
00:05:51.858 --> 00:05:58.582
By this point, Tom could hardly breathe, for fear he would make another mistake.

68
00:05:58.583 --> 00:06:02.705
He caught sight of Marlow, standing at the back of the room.

69
00:06:02.706 --> 00:06:09.978
Marlow gave him an encouraging smile, and Tom remembered their first conversation.

70
00:06:09.979 --> 00:06:17.725
"Now that you're king," Marlow had said, "you can do whatever you want."

71
00:06:17.726 --> 00:06:24.955
Tom opened his mouth and out came a tremendous blast of sound.

72
00:06:24.956 --> 00:06:42.546
He laughed as the noise from the trumpeter's horn covered his burp.

